{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1505112707,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUyNTY1OTg0NjY=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1819","origin":"github"},"title":"NEEDED: Convention for referring to a dataset vs. a directory for path arg input","message":"As discussed briefly during last meeting: Some commands (one of them being `publish`, another `metadata`) have to distinguish user input referring to a directory (i.e. dataset content) vs. a dataset itself. As we are only using paths this distinction is difficult and leads to inflation of the API with disambiguating options.\n\nWe should try to come up with a convention how to identify a dataset via a path, in a way that is different from the directory in is in. It has to be the dataset that gets special markup, because we do not want to be the root of a (sub)dataset to behave differently from any other directory in a dataset.\n\nIf found, this convention should then get detected during path annotation.","files":null}]}